1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,130
Let's go for a walk.

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:07,970
Let's go.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:08,860
Sea Talk.

4
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,840
(Sea Talk rules)
Late-night heart-to-hearts.

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,180
(Looks)

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,600
You actually pried that shell off?

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,920
It had this little light,

8
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,160
so I thought

9
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,960
there had to be

10
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,760
some kind of sign.

11
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,800
But I couldn't find one.

12
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,280
So I thought that piece
was how you started it.

13
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:31,840
I figured I had to...

14
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,040
You thought it was a switch?

15
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:33,480
Yeah.

16
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,400
I thought I'd get something

17
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,080
to show that I'd started it.

18
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:39,180
(Takes it)

19
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,840
I'd been thinking about it for days.

20
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:44,660
We were almost at the end.

21
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:45,870
I didn't want to leave with regrets.

22
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,820
I knew how I felt,

23
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:49,730
but I didn't know where Si stood.

24
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,330
So I decided to do a Sea Talk.

25
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,080
And...

26
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,400
it felt kind of special.

27
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,440
And honestly,

28
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,000
I just...

29
00:00:59,000 --> 00:00:59,800
I mean...

30
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:02,400
I hadn't tried it yet.

31
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,560
I was also waiting for a night

32
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
when she wouldn't be too tired.

33
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,840
She got back late every night.

34
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:07,680
And time was running out.

35
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,360
We only had a few days left.

36
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,120
If I didn't do it, then...

37
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,040
You'd miss your chance.

38
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,040
Yeah, so I went for it.

39
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:16,600
The vibe was really nice.

40
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,000
It gave us some space to...

41
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,720
Really talk.

42
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,600
Yeah, to say what was on our minds.

43
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,360
Did that charm you a little?

44
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,000
Yeah, it did.

45
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,600
Why are you smiling?

46
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,600
Nothing.

47
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,480
I'm just shy.

48
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:34,820
(Hands it over)

49
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,360
That shell?

50
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,030
Really? Why'd you give her that?

51
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:40,560
That one, right?

52
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,560
(Hands it over)
No, not that one.

53
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,360
Wasn't that the prop you broke?

54
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,600
That was the only thing there.

55
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,400
Si didn't notice anything weird.

56
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,040
She just took it.

57
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:48,960
You just took it like it was nothing.

58
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,960
I noticed. It still had glue underneath.

59
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,720
There was glue underneath?

60
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,160
I just love

61
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:54,960
this little thing

62
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,240
you two have going on.

63
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,280
It's so cute.

64
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,080
And Si

65
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,640
had just as many little expressions

66
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,600
as you did.

67
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,920
She had tons.

68
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:02,960
It's all in those little looks.

69
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,640
She'd glance over at you,

70
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,240
check you out,

71
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,960
then get all shy.

72
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,760
Exactly.

73
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:12,710
That outfit you're wearing

74
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:14,360
is actually perfect

75
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,430
for starting this.

76
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,760
There, you looked at me again.

77
00:02:17,790 --> 00:02:18,760
Yeah, starting the car.

78
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:21,130
Starting what?

79
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:22,400
The car?

80
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,110
No, I said starting Sea Talk.

81
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,400
You two misheard each other again.

82
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:27,340
(Looks)

83
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:27,960
Dragonfly.

84
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,040
They're everywhere.

85
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:30,420
(Turns)

86
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,620
(Looks away)

87
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,140
(Looks down, smiles)

88
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:36,100
(Looks)

89
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,590
Why are you smiling?

90
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:38,800
Why are you?

91
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,680
Why are you smiling?

92
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,240
How do I put this...

93
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,000
I suddenly got nervous.

94
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:48,530
Let's go down.

95
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,600
You walked like an old man.

96
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:54,400
Hands behind your back.

97
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,840
It was awkward.

98
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:56,720
Really awkward.

99
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,840
I didn't know where to put my hands.

100
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,120
I wanted to reach out...

101
00:02:59,120 --> 00:02:59,560
Put it there.

102
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,280
Now you know.

103
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:00,880
Where? Right here?

104
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:01,720
Now you know.

105
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:02,400
I didn't know back then.

106
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,280
Need a hand?

107
00:03:05,290 --> 00:03:06,680
See? You knew where to put your hands.

108
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,640
Wait, there was this part too?

109
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:09,400
So you did know.

110
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,480
No, I didn't.

111
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,510
There's a mirror.

112
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:14,970
Want to check yourself?

113
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,050
Let's do it together.

114
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:16,560
Together?

115
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,540
(Together)

116
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:19,990
My hair is a mess.

117
00:03:19,990 --> 00:03:20,750
You look good.

118
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:21,620
Even cuter like that.

119
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:22,620
(Even cuter)

120
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:23,640
See?

121
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,800
You would never

122
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,040
leave Si hanging.

123
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,380
(Sneaks a glance)

124
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,300
(Eye contact)

125
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:35,930
You two could do this all day.

126
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:39,540
(Looks up)

127
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,120
What are you doing, Mr. Cui?

128
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,320
Was it awkward for you two?

129
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,360
A little.

130
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,520
We were just so close.

131
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,640
If I feel like

132
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:55,560
there's real potential
and he could be...

133
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:57,720
the right person,

134
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:00,850
I don't need to know everything
about him yet.

135
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:02,800
If we click

136
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,880
and feel comfortable together,

137
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,490
I'm open

138
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:07,720
to giving it a shot.

139
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,380
(Laughs)

140
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:10,120
He's so happy.

141
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,540
Mr. Cui, you...

142
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,140
As for me, I don't really

143
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:13,260
have a set pace in mind.

144
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,080
Are you ever going to stop smiling?

145
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:15,800
Exactly.

146
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,070
(Eye contact)

147
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:18,580
What's with that little smile?

148
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,680
Little? He's been grinning
this whole time.

149
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,800
I'm not even hiding it.

150
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:27,530
We're almost at the end, right?

151
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:29,930
What if

152
00:04:29,930 --> 00:04:31,230
there's one final choice?

153
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,700
Same cards as last time.

154
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,330
And...

155
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:37,940
(Smiles)

156
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:39,030
Basically, you'd be choosing

157
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:40,960
how you want your journey

158
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,760
to end.

159
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:46,280
Don't do that.

160
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:47,640
What's wrong?

161
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,040
Your eyebrows hurt?

162
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,000
So you wanted to ask Si

163
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:51,840
if she'd choose

164
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:52,960
option A or B?

165
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:53,500
Yeah,

166
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,080
but I was too shy to ask.

167
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:54,400
Right?

168
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,800
Yeah, pretty much.

169
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:58,000
Don't act all shy now.

170
00:04:59,240 --> 00:04:59,920
Before we started,

171
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,800
you were sitting like this.

172
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:01,840
Now look at you.

173
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:02,840
Exactly.

174
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,480
Let's continue.

175
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,050
I think...

176
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:13,600
If I could choose again,

177
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,900
I'd probably pick the red ticket.

178
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,620
(I'd pick the red ticket)

179
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,320
Goosebumps again.

180
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,200
So satisfying.

181
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,200
So,

182
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,040
did you already know
where this was going?

183
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,840
Not really.

184
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,160
I just felt a little more sure.

185
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,240
Because

186
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,080
we didn't really talk

187
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:30,880
about this much.

188
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,000
We just went by feel.

189
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,040
We barely said anything out loud.

190
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,800
I had no idea where your head was at.

191
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,760
You never said anything.

192
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,040
You never asked.

193
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,120
That's on me.

194
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,040
I was the one who didn't ask.

195
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,440
Yeah, I should've asked.

196
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:46,120
I was just worried that if I asked...

197
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,400
Like, if I brought it up

198
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,480
and it wasn't...

199
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,600
Maybe things just weren't there yet,

200
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,560
and it felt too soon.

201
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,720
If you brought it up then,

202
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,280
she might overthink it.

203
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:52,840
Yeah. I kept waiting for...

204
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:53,960
She might feel pressured, too.

205
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,240
Right, I was waiting
for the right moment

206
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,040
to bring it up.

207
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:56,560
I was...

208
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,080
hoping I'd only have to ask once.

209
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,520
Wait, no.

210
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,640
Only once?

211
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,800
There it is. The truth comes out.

212
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,480
I wanted to get it right in one shot.

213
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,400
No back-and-forth.

214
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,560
If I kept asking,

215
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,640
the second time would feel different.

216
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,040
But that time, I had no choice.

217
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,480
It was really almost over.

218
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,720
I felt like I had to ask.

219
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,400
I couldn't keep letting her get her way.

220
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,300
No.

221
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:16,960
She was the one who let me have my way.

222
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:17,520
My way.

223
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:20,970
Do you mean last time or this time?

224
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,100
If we're talking about this time...

225
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,900
(This time, I'm sure about you)

226
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,560
You know what it felt like?

227
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,120
Like making a little kid laugh.

228
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,600
She'd tease him, and he'd smile.

229
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,160
Then she'd do it again,
and he'd smile again.

230
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,160
I couldn't help it.

231
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:40,760
I was genuinely

232
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:41,440
happy.

233
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,120
She was pretty sleepy, though.

234
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,720
It was really late.

235
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,400
You did that on purpose.

236
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,320
You waited until she was half asleep

237
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,120
before asking her that.

238
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:50,640
Maybe a little.

239
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,000
You had it all planned out,
straight out of The Art of War.

240
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:52,960
No.

241
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:53,600
It's Cui's Art of War.

242
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,360
Cui's Art of War?

243
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,080
I'm kidding.

244
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,160
Learned that from Sun?

245
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:00,760
The one next to you?

246
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,240
Sun's Art of War.

247
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:04,960
He's read it,

248
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:05,920
but that's about it.

249
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:07,600
Just kidding.

250
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:09,800
You like this part?

251
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,880
I totally forgot about this.

252
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,200
Not me. I remember it.

253
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,840
That memorable?

254
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,080
Very.

255
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,840
My heart was pounding that night.

256
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,640
Really?

257
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:20,960
I was so nervous.

258
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,000
I didn't know how to bring it up.

259
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,440
No wonder.

260
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,200
I thought all that noise

261
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,000
in the bushes was an animal.

262
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,080
Turns out it was your heartbeat.

263
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,400
I still remember

264
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,840
his face when he asked.

265
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,200
What face?

266
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,480
He just...

267
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,720
wouldn't even look at me.

268
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,760
I was too nervous.

269
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:39,120
You know?

270
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,520
And Si was giving me this sleepy look.

271
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,240
Like...

272
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,760
I thought she was flirting with me.

273
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,200
So

274
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,400
I got a little braver.

275
00:07:49,580 --> 00:07:51,140
(Sun Bohan)

276
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,520
Hello, Xing.

277
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:54,710
(Smiles)

278
00:07:54,710 --> 00:07:55,330
What are you doing?

279
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:56,560
How's the pain now?

280
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,660
Has the anesthesia worn off?

281
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,400
Not feeling much now, right?

282
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,720
She was so thin then.

283
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,640
Yeah, really thin.

284
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,140
She was living on liquids.

285
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:05,820
Anyone would lose weight.

286
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,040
Xing, were you able to walk by then?

287
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,080
Just a couple of steps.

288
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:09,640
Yeah, I could walk.

289
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:11,270
I asked the doctor.

290
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:12,890
He said 100 mL of water

291
00:08:12,890 --> 00:08:14,320
with six scoops, right?

292
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,750
I'll heat it to about 45°C,

293
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,190
then mix it.

294
00:08:19,190 --> 00:08:20,700
